# Circutor CVM-MINI.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Circutor CVM-MINI — DIN-Rail 3-Phase Power Analyzer (Modbus RTU RS-485)
# | 
# | Source: circutor-cvm-mini-instruction-manual.pdf (section 6, pp. 23-26)
# | Models: CVM-MINI (base), CVM-MINI-HAR (+ harmonics up to 15th order)
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU, FC03/04 read, FC01 relay read, FC05 relay write
# | Baud: configurable (default 9600 8N1)
# | All MODBUS addresses are hexadecimal in source; converted to decimal here.
# | All parameters are s32 (2 consecutive registers, 32-bit signed).
# | Scaling: V×10, current in mA, Hz×10, kvar/kVA in W, PF×100, THD %×10.
# | Harmonics registers (HAR model only): RMS = s32 (Vx10 or mA); harmonics 2-15 = s32 (%).
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Circutor
@model=CVM-MINI
@description=DIN-rail 3-phase power analyzer, Modbus RTU RS-485. FC03/04 read, FC01/FC05 relay. All params s32. Phase V(×10)/I(mA)/P/Q/PF per phase + 3-phase totals (addr 0-84). Energy (Wh) at 60-94. THD at 48-58. HAR model: voltage harmonics 1-15 for L1/L2/L3 at 686-774; current harmonics 1-15 at 500-588.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/circutor-cvm-mini.toml; Source: circutor-cvm-mini-instruction-manual.pdf (section 6, pp. 23-26). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
